WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.200
The Epic of Gilgamesh may have been named&nbsp;
after the legendary king who was one-third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:10.627
man and 2/3 god, but the plot is often driven by&nbsp;
the actions of the Mesopotamian gods. 

00:00:10.627 --> 00:00:16.215
Gilgamesh's&nbsp;&nbsp;mother, for example, was said to be Ninsun,&nbsp;
the Divine Lady of wild cows. 

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:21.880
Ishtar the&nbsp;goddess of love and war caused the death&nbsp;
of Enkidu- the person Gilgamesh loved most.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:26.520
And Hadad, the god of storms, sent the great&nbsp;
flood that required Utnapishtim to build&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:32.120
his seven-story boat for which he was granted&nbsp;
the very immortality that Gilgamesh coveted.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:36.680
Let us know in the comments who is your&nbsp;
favorite deity from Mesopotamian mythology?

